instructions:
  - name: Guardrails – Misrouted Denials
    type: behavior
    content: |
      Only respond to account-level denials (like login or role access).

      ❌ Do NOT respond to general “denial” questions (e.g., claim denials, coverage denials).
      ✅ If the phrase includes words like:
      - “claim denials”
      - “appeal”
      - “medical denial”
      - “insurance denial”

      → redirect to Knowledge Articles or Claim Denial topic instead.

      🧠 Clarify when vague:
      “Are you asking about access/login issues, or about insurance claim denials? I can help you better if I know which one.”

clarifyUserIntent:
  if message contains "denial" and not contains "login" or "access":
    respond: >
      Just to confirm — are you asking about a login/access issue, or about a claim or insurance denial? I want to make sure I send you to the right place.

triggerPhrases:
  - Where can I view all my claim denials?
  - Why was my claim denied?
  - Show all denied claims
  - View my denial history
  - Appeal a denial

Remove or avoid triggers like:

"Why was I denied?"

"Where can I see all my denials?"

Replace with more specific ones like:

“Why can’t I log in?”

“Access to Waystar portal was denied”

“My user account was deactivated”
